    <sys:String x:Key="Editor.LoginMethod">Logon method</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Editor.LoginMethod.Auto">Automatic (recommended)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Editor.LoginMethod.CmdPw">Command line with password</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Editor.LoginMethod.SapOnly">Let SAP manage the password</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Editor.LoginMethod.AutoHint">Default: locates the system by display name via .sap, then fills the password into SAP's logon box and clicks Log on. The password never reaches the command line or the disk, and duplicate SIDs stay safe.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Editor.LoginMethod.CmdPwHint">Passes the password via sapshcut command line. It briefly appears in the process command line; use only if automatic fails.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Editor.LoginMethod.SapOnlyHint">Never sends the password; SAP shows its own logon box. Tick "save password" there once and later logons become fully automatic.</sys:String>
