    <sys:String x:Key="Settings.ClearCreds">Clear all credentials</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Settings.AllowCmdPw">Allow password on the command line</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Settings.AllowCmdPwHint">Off by default. The main path is "locate via .sap + auto-fill the logon box", so the password never reaches the command line or the disk. This is an extreme fallback only: when on, the password briefly appears in the sapshcut process command line.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Settings.Launch">Logon</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Settings.DefaultClient">Default client</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Settings.WorkDir">SAP working directory</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Settings.Reuse">Reuse existing session</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Settings.AutoFillLogon">Auto-fill the SAP logon dialog</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Settings.AutoFillLogonHint">Since SAP GUI 7.40 the password in .sap files is ignored, so the "Shortcut - Logon" dialog shows up often. When enabled, the password is filled in and Logon is clicked only if the dialog belongs to a process inside the SAP installation folder and its system/client match the current target. At most one fill per logon attempt: retrying a rejected password can lock the account.</sys:String>
